    howToApply: "CONSUMING a set: ask what single search produced it and whether it would have reached a member spelled differently. Re-derive cheaply: search again in a way the author plainly did not (another name, the declaration rather than the call), and check each named member exists. AUTHORING a set: do not write the universal; scope the sentence to the search ('the six places this search found'), and name something as existing only after reading it in code.",
