    howToApply: "When judging a friction item, first trace each citation to the claim: does it substantiate the lesson, or just sit beside it? It fails here even if real. Then: reconstructible means nothing to graduate; prefer editing the nearest note; hold back when unsure; a one-off waits for it to recur (reinforce); prefer a tool or code fix over prose to remember. Record the verdict and its reasons on the friction item (route).",
